    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43857" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐερνής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρνος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sprouting well, flourishing</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάφνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					1100
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); of a kind of Cassia, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.13
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δένδρον-έστατον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.629
				</span></i>
			; of men and animals, <i>well-grown</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Posidon.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				28
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			), <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				11.4.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				314.10
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Smyrna</span>): 
				Comp.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έστερα</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, νήπια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					17(1).826
				</span></i>
			; of countries, <i>rich in plants</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔβοτος καὶ εὐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				16.1.24
			</span></i>.</div>
